---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro"
import HeroMedia from "../../components/HeroMedia.astro"
import SectionHeader from "../../components/SectionHeader.astro"
import FullWidthText from "../../components/FullWidthText.astro"
import TextImageRow from "../../components/TextImageRow.astro"
import MediaGrid from "../../components/MediaGrid.astro"
import PageTitle from "../../components/PageTitle.astro"
---

<Layout>
    <div class="content">


        <PageTitle 
         title="Eye To Eye - VFX Short Film"
         />

        <HeroMedia
            src="/media/Eye_To_Eye_CG.mp4"
            alt="Eye to Eye CG"
            type="video"
        />
    
        <FullWidthText>
            <p>
            <br>
            Eye to Eye was one of the films I worked on during my second year at the University of Hertfordshire.
            As a freelance TD, I was responsible for producing the lighting for all CG shots, as well as acting as  
            a point of contact to troubleshoot any technical challenges that arose during production.
            <br><br>
            
            As a lighting TD, my focus was on matching the style and visual direction established by the core team with 
            one of the most prominent references being Lost Ollie. I aimed to create lighting that kept the character  
            grounded and believable, while still preserving that sense of childlike wonder and magic that was so crucial
            to the film's identity.
            <br><br>

            </p>
        </FullWidthText>

    </div>
</Layout>

